---
/**
 * Privacy Policy (EN) — /privacy/
 *
 * Discloses:
 *   1. Zero data collection & zero data retention in the LiveAudio desktop app (100% local)
 *   2. Outbound Network Scope (Desktop App): on-demand SHA-256 models, optional 24h update check, opt-in CUDA runtime
 *   3. Website-only analytics: Microsoft Clarity (heatmaps, session replay, _clck, _clsk, privacy statement link)
 *   4. Data rights and contact information
 */
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { localizedPath } from "../i18n/routes";
import { REPO_URL, ISSUES_URL } from "../config/release";

const path = localizedPath("en", "privacy");
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — LiveAudio"
  description="Privacy Policy for LiveAudio and liveaudio.opencohost.com. The LiveAudio desktop app collects zero data and retains zero data — audio and transcripts never leave your machine. Only the website uses Microsoft Clarity."
  eyebrow="COMPLIANCE · LEGAL"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="Last updated: November 2026"
  badge="ZERO APP DATA · 100% LOCAL"
  lang="en"
  path={path}
>
  <div class="callout-signal">
    <h2>
      <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Zero Data Collection &amp; 100% Local Audio Processing
    </h2>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not collect or retain any user data in the LiveAudio desktop app</strong> — running 100% locally is the
      core benefit of LiveAudio. All speech recognition, audio capture, and AI inference (NVIDIA Parakeet-TDT and Whisper)
      execute strictly on your device's local hardware (CPU, DirectML DirectX 12 GPU, or optional NVIDIA CUDA via CTranslate2).
      <strong>Audio and transcripts never leave your machine.</strong> Only this website
      (<code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code>) uses Microsoft Clarity for web analytics.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Overview and Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Plynte Labs ("we", "us", or "our") handles information in connection with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The LiveAudio Desktop Application:</strong> The free, open-source (MIT) downloadable software for Windows x64 and
      Linux x86_64 that generates real-time captions locally and streams them to OBS over a local WebSocket. The desktop app
      collects zero data and retains zero data on our servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The LiveAudio Website:</strong> The marketing and documentation site hosted at <code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code>,
      which is the only surface that uses Microsoft Clarity web analytics.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. LiveAudio Desktop Application — Zero Data Collection &amp; Retention</h2>
  <p>
    The LiveAudio desktop software collects zero personal information, retains zero user data on external servers, and never
    records, transmits, or monetizes your audio streams, transcripts, settings, or usage:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero Audio Transmission:</strong> Audio captured from your microphone or system-audio loopback (Windows WASAPI or
      Linux PipeWire/PulseAudio monitor capture with ALSA fallback) is processed in memory on your machine and discarded after
      transcription frames are generated.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local Model Inference:</strong> ONNX Runtime models (Parakeet &amp; Whisper) and optional CTranslate2 weights are
      stored on your local drive and run entirely on your own CPU, DirectML (DirectX 12 GPU), or optional NVIDIA CUDA
      (CTranslate2).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local-Only WebSocket:</strong> LiveAudio broadcasts transcription events over a local WebSocket server binding
      exclusively to <code>127.0.0.1</code> (default port <code>8765</code>) with a loopback Origin allowlist. This connection
      stays strictly local to your workstation unless you explicitly configure remote tunneling on your own infrastructure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Zero Telemetry &amp; Local-Only Storage:</strong> Session transcripts (<code>.srt</code>, <code>.vtt</code>,
      <code>.jsonl</code>), settings, and usage counters live solely on your local disk. The application contains no analytics
      SDKs, no usage telemetry, and no automated crash-reporting daemons.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Outbound Network Scope (Desktop App)</h2>
  <p>
    The LiveAudio desktop app makes outbound network connections strictly for the following user-visible purposes — and never
    transmits audio, transcripts, or telemetry:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>On-demand model downloads:</strong> Parakeet-TDT ONNX and Whisper models are downloaded from official model hosts
      when you select a model that is not yet cached locally, and every download is SHA-256 verified before use.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Optional 24-hour GitHub Releases update check:</strong> The app can check GitHub Releases metadata once every
      24 hours to notify you of newer versions (zero telemetry; toggleable at any time in <strong>Settings &gt; Advanced</strong>).
      Signed in-app updates (Minisign Ed25519 on Windows NSIS and Linux <code>.AppImage</code>) are stream-safe and never apply
      while transcription is live or OBS is connected.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Opt-in NVIDIA CUDA runtime download:</strong> The optional CTranslate2 CUDA worker (<code>ct2-worker</code>) and
      cuBLAS/cuDNN runtime libraries are downloaded only if you explicitly opt in from Settings.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Audio and transcripts never leave your machine.</strong> Once your chosen models are cached locally, transcription
    operates completely offline.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Website Information Collection &amp; Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Only this website (<code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code>) collects web analytics.</strong> When you browse the
    documentation or marketing pages, we use Microsoft Clarity exclusively to understand how visitors navigate the site,
    diagnose usability issues, and improve documentation. We do not run any other analytics provider on this website, we do not
    require account registration, and we do not collect personal identifiers like names, physical addresses, or financial details.
  </p>

  <h3>Microsoft Clarity Integration (Website Only)</h3>
  <p>
    We partner with Microsoft Clarity and Microsoft Advertising on <code>liveaudio.opencohost.com</code> to capture how you
    use and interact with our website through behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and session replay to improve our website and
    documentation. Website usage data is captured using first- and third-party cookies and other tracking technologies to
    understand site activity, improve usability, and support security and fraud prevention.
  </p>
  <p>
    Microsoft Clarity sets the following first-party cookies in your browser when visiting this website:
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Cookie</th>
          <th>Provider</th>
          <th>Duration</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_clck</code></td>
          <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
          <td>1 year</td>
          <td>Persists the unique Clarity user ID and browser settings across page navigation on the same domain.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_clsk</code></td>
          <td>Microsoft Clarity</td>
          <td>1 day</td>
          <td>Connects individual page views into a single recorded session and tracks user interaction flow.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Clarity records website interactions such as mouse clicks, mouse movements, scrolling, and aggregate viewport dimensions.
    Sensitive text inputs and confidential form fields are automatically masked by Clarity prior to transmission.
    For more details on how Microsoft collects and processes data, please review the
    <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cookies &amp; Tracking Management</h2>
  <p>
    You can manage, restrict, or delete website cookies at any time through your web browser preferences. Most modern browsers allow you to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Block third-party cookies or all cookies altogether.</li>
    <li>Delete existing cookies upon closing your browser session.</li>
    <li>Use private browsing or incognito windows to prevent long-term tracking.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can also learn how to opt out of Microsoft personalized advertising by visiting the
    <a href="https://account.microsoft.com/privacy/ad-settings" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Ad Settings page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention &amp; Security</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Desktop application:</strong> We retain zero user data because the LiveAudio desktop app collects zero data and
    never sends your audio, transcripts, or settings to our servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Website:</strong> Aggregated website analytics data collected by Microsoft Clarity is retained in accordance with
    Microsoft Clarity's standard data retention policies (typically 30 to 90 days for session recordings). We protect the website
    infrastructure using strict Content-Security-Policy (CSP) headers, enforced HTTPS encryption (TLS 1.3), and immutable asset hashing.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Open Source Code Transparency</h2>
  <p>
    Because LiveAudio is an open-source project licensed under the MIT License, our application code is publicly auditable.
    You can inspect the entire Rust audio pipeline, WebSocket server, ONNX Runtime (Parakeet &amp; Whisper) worker, and update
    checker in our
    <a href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository</a>
    to verify that no audio, transcripts, or telemetry leave your computer.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on your location (including the European Economic Area, the UK, and California), you may have rights under applicable data protection
    laws (such as GDPR or CCPA/CPRA), including the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data collected about you.
    Because we do not collect data in the desktop app and do not store customer profiles or identifiable personal records on our website, we may
    require additional contextual information to locate any relevant anonymized website analytics records.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions, feedback, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or our local-first privacy practices, please contact us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:gitrafuh@gmail.com">gitrafuh@gmail.com</a></li>
    <li><strong>Project Issues:</strong> <a href={ISSUES_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/plynte-labs/LiveAudio/issues</a></li>
    <li><strong>Organization:</strong> Plynte Labs</li>
  </ul>
</LegalPage>
